**This side:** no repository path is written, so no file set is held. The only writes are Jira (four comments, three tickets, three label adds) and files under `.tools/b1163/`, `Briefs/2026-11-03_B1163_STATUS.md` and the Step-0 copy of this kit. **Other side:** open pull requests at drafting: `datasecau/HPSM-POC` 0 and `datasecau/HPSM-POC-analysis` 0 (`gh api -X GET repos/<repo>/pulls -f state=open`, control `pulls/99999` 404); the parked focus-ring branch (the one ref under `refs/heads/b1097/`) is read only through the gate's STATUS and is not touched; the only other live panes are `Datasec/Security-Composer-G300` and `Datasec/MPS-M81` (other projects, no shared key, file or label); no seat is commissioned on HPSMPOC-417, -436, -407 or -399 (the tuesday briefs folder holds no other 2026-11-03 HPSM-POC kit: its 2026-11-03 kits are B1162 and B1164, both MPS, and the sweep; `/usr/bin/grep -l -E 'HPSMPOC-436|HPSMPOC-399'` over the 2026-11-02 and 2026-11-03 files lists the finished kits B1097, B1098, B1110 and B1122, the board screen SCREEN-1745, the sweeps and this kit; none of those four seats has a pane). Re-read at Step 0 and before the first Jira write.

## HOLDS
Transitions: none, on any key. No reopen; no description, label or priority edit on an existing key (the one label add is on a ticket this seat created); no link; no create beyond the three tickets; no comment on any key but -417, -436, -407 and -399, and none on a new key. No statement that anyone has been told, that a words question is settled, that the page movement is accepted or rejected, that anything is deployed, that a host runs any of it, or that main is green. **This phase builds no integration with HP tools (Security Manager API, Fleet Threat Assessment, firmware tools, SIEM); next-phase items are stored and architected only, never shown to HP as done** (in no Jira or record text). PRIOR-WORK CHECK first: a final line without a `PRIOR WORK` section is returned unread. No message to any human (no mail, chat, board post, PR). **Never delete** (quarantine to `.tools/b1163/_quarantine/`); never type `cd`, `rm` or `sed -i`; absolute single-quoted paths (`!` in the project path); `/usr/bin/grep -i` with a positive control for every count; `python3 -I -B`; never print a token, key or login; never run `du` over `.tools`. `git` read verbs only in the project repository and the records repository (`gh api -X GET` for the code and records repositories, under the project `GH_CONFIG_DIR`); the single exception is `git init` and `git add` inside `.tools/b1163/main-copy` (Step 2). No HTTP to any hosted, demo or production host, not even GET (the GitHub API and archive via `gh`, and Jira, only). No write to `2_Project_Files`, any product, test or infra file, the records repository, `*_evidence/`, UAT, the demo, Azure. **Read no decision card** (the product owner's question on the page movement is open; J4 only records the measurement). If a Jira write fails or reads back unequal: stop that item, fix the root cause, re-verify; never retry a POST or a create blindly (read the project first: a create that returned an error may still have landed). A figure or a pointer that fails its source HOLDS the text that carries it.
**Not yours:** every other HPSMPOC key, `2_Project_Files`, the code repository (GET only), the records repository (GET only), the root working copy (stale), every `.git/config`, the decision store, the demo, Azure, and the other seats' `.tools/` directories except to `cp` the named helpers.

## UNMEASURED by the drafter
No write of any kind; the Bicep binary's version and whether it runs; whether the suite is green here (the drafter ran none of it); the hosted runner's python; whether the 10-minute foreground limit is enough on this machine; whether `git add -A -f` of the extracted copy reproduces `git ls-files` of the real repository (the file-count equality is the check, line-ending and mode differences are not); what a live model returns for an empty finding explanation; what the stored narrative and the reader's screen show after the refusal; whether any caller sends an empty list; the product owner's reading of the page movement; whether the census figures of gate B1130 were measured on a ref that still exists (the branch is parked, not read here); the J2, J3 and J4 texts' fit to the screen the ticket's reader uses.

